      "date": "2026-11-14 01:19:46.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 5:\n\n(6 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nSome concerns, see inline comments. The per-function summary only works when a single .c file is selected, and the dependency reload runs even without -g.\n\nSeparately, collect_gcov(), print_gcov_summary(), the gcov/gcov-tool checks and the merge-skip logic that this commit message describes are already in the parent change (\"kunit: add ku runner, KUNIT.list and KUNIT.modules_list\"). There, $GCOV is never set, so every run prints \"[: : integer expected\". Should those pieces move into this patch so that each change stands on its own?",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 5
    },
